  "question": {
    "text": "The equation of the plane containing the line \\(\\frac{\\mathrm{x}-\\mathrm{x}_1}{\\ell}=\\frac{\\mathrm{y}-\\mathrm{y}_1}{\\mathrm{~m}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{z}-\\mathrm{z}_1}{\\mathrm{n}}\\) is \\(a\\left(x-x_1\\right)+b\\left(y-y_1\\right)+c\\left(z-z_1\\right)=0\\), then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "3ntom",
      "text": "\\(\\mathrm{ax}_1+\\mathrm{by}_1+\\mathrm{cz}_1=0\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ELGYU",
      "text": "\\(a \\ell+b m+c n=0\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "jw90Q",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{\\mathrm{a}}{\\ell}=\\frac{\\mathrm{b}}{\\mathrm{m}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{c}}{\\mathrm{n}}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "qHtRX",
      "text": "\\(\\ell \\mathrm{x}_1+\\mathrm{my}_1+\\mathrm{nz}_1=0\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "If the given plane contains the given line then the normal to the plane, must be perpendicular to the line and the condition for the same is \\(a \\ell+b m+c n=0\\).",
    "image": null
  },
